4:["$","article",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-2","children":[["$","span","GST",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"GST"}],["$","span","Invoicing",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"Invoicing"}],["$","span","India",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"India"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl","children":"How to Create a GST Invoice in India (Step-by-Step Guide)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300","children":"Learn how to create GST invoice in India with GST invoice format, examples, CGST/SGST/IGST, PDF templates, mistakes and FAQs."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500","children":["20 May 2026"," · ",18," min read · ","InvoiceWala Team"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-10","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-invert max-w-none prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-cyan-300","children":[["$","h2","0",{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-white","children":"What is a GST Invoice?"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"A GST invoice is a tax invoice issued by a GST registered business when it supplies taxable goods or services. It records what was sold, who sold it, who bought it, the taxable value, the GST rate, the GST amount and the final invoice value. In simple words, a GST invoice is both a payment request and a tax record."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"For Indian businesses, a GST invoice is important because it creates a clear trail for sales, tax calculation, customer records and payment follow-up. It also helps B2B buyers claim Input Tax Credit, commonly called ITC, when they are eligible. If the invoice is missing GSTIN, tax breakup, invoice number or correct customer details, the buyer may face problems while matching records."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"A good GST invoice should be easy to read. Your customer should quickly understand your business details, their billing details, what items or services were charged, how GST was calculated and how much they need to pay. This is why GST invoice format matters. The format keeps your invoice structured and reduces mistakes."}]]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"GST compliance does not mean the invoice has to look complicated. A freelancer invoice, contractor invoice, service business invoice and product invoice can all follow the same basic structure: supplier details, buyer details, invoice details, item table, tax breakup, total amount, notes and payment terms. The exact fields may change depending on your business type, place of supply and customer type."}]]}],["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"If you are creating your first GST invoice, the easiest approach is to use a "}],["$","$L7","1",{"className":"font-semibold text-cyan-300 underline-offset-2 hover:underline","href":"/gst-invoice-generator","children":"GST invoice generator"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". You can enter business details, add customer information, add item rows, apply tax, preview the GST invoice PDF and download a professional invoice without manually fixing formulas in Excel."}]]}],"$L9","$La","$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L